In this unit, we will use limits to introduce one of the central idea of this course: the derivative.
To motivate the idea, let’s consider the idea of instantaneous speed. If we know how far something has traveled over a given interval of time, we can calculate \[\frac{\text{Distance Traveled}}{\text{Duration}}\] This quantity tells us how fast the object was traveling on average throughout the time interval. Is it possible to determine how fast the object was traveling at a specific moment?

